# Guardian-Unit-Penetration-Testing Agent's own rule definitions contain, by necessity, literal examples of
# every pattern they detect. Scanning them reports the detector as the defect.
# Every security scanner needs an exclusion like this one; ours is checked in
# so you can see exactly what we exempt and why.
src/scanners
src/data

# The redaction tests must contain real-shaped credentials, because that is
# what they assert never reaches an output. Guardian-Unit-Penetration-Testing Agent correctly finds them and
# correctly downgrades them to test-context severity; excluded here so our own
# scan is clean rather than because the detection is wrong.
test

# Deliberately vulnerable demonstration code. Scanned on purpose, by name,
# never as part of a scan of the repository.
examples/vulnerable-app

# Research reports quoting vulnerable example code.
docs
